WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.664
The sample's shape is right,

2
00:00:01.664 --> 00:00:05.112
and the code keeps it as the
model for the location policy.

3
00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:06.900
But the values aren't values.

4
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.755
The state field is literally the text
"enabled or disabled", and the service

5
00:00:11.755 --> 00:00:16.450
principal ID is a placeholder in
brackets, so Graph refuses it outright.

6
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.512
Worse, the easy ways to
fill it in are dangerous.

7
00:00:19.512 --> 00:00:24.387
One option covers every service
principal in the tenant, reviewed or not.

8
00:00:24.387 --> 00:00:28.262
Another trusts every network you've
marked trusted for people, too.

9
00:00:28.262 --> 00:00:32.705
The code allows only reviewed
object IDs and one dedicated,

10
00:00:32.705 --> 00:00:34.750
untrusted named location.
